Rubric
 The two biggest categories of lung disease that cause bronchoconstriction/bronchospasm are COPD (chronic obstructive pulmonary disease) and asthma.  Bronchitis is one other one that could be mentioned.  In both of these cases the lower airways are affected and the bronchospasm occurs from the contraction of the smooth muscle in the walls of the bronchioles.  Mucus production can further exacerbate the symptoms but is not what is responsible for the actual spasm or contraction of the bronchioles.  The most common symptoms associated with either disease process (COPD or asthma) include wheezing, tachypnea, retractions, dyspnea when speaking and sitting in a tripod position  

